---@field condition? string The condition expressions to evaluate. If the condition evaluates to true, the overrides or fixed_response in this rule will be applied. An empty condition is always true. For more details on condition expressions, please see https://developers.cloudflare.com/load-balancing/understand-basics/load-balancing-rules/expressions.
---@field disabled? boolean Disable this specific rule. It will no longer be evaluated by this load balancer.
---@field fixed_response? cloudflare.load_balancers.CreateRequestRulesItemFixedResponse A collection of fields used to directly respond to the client instead of routing to a pool. When supplied on a rule, that rule stops further rule evaluation.
---@field name? string Name of this rule. Only used for human readability.
---@field overrides? cloudflare.load_balancers.CreateRequestRulesItemOverrides A collection of overrides to apply when this rule's condition (or a pool set's `match`) is true. All fields are optional.
---@field priority? number The order in which rules should be executed in relation to each other. Lower values are executed first. Values do not need to be sequential. If all priorities are omitted or zero, the API assigns priorities based on the array order of the rules field.
---@field terminates? boolean If this rule's condition is true, this causes rule evaluation to stop after processing this rule.

