---@class cloudflare.load_balancers.GetMonitorResponse
---@field id? string|distilled.Null
---@field allow_insecure? boolean|distilled.Null Do not validate the certificate when monitor use HTTPS. This parameter is currently only valid for HTTP and HTTPS monitors.
---@field consecutive_down? number|distilled.Null To be marked unhealthy the monitored origin must fail this healthcheck N consecutive times.
---@field consecutive_up? number|distilled.Null To be marked healthy the monitored origin must pass this healthcheck N consecutive times.
---@field created_on? string|distilled.Null
---@field description? string|distilled.Null Object description.
---@field expected_body? string|distilled.Null A case-insensitive sub-string to look for in the response body. If this string is not found, the origin will be marked as unhealthy. This parameter is only valid for HTTP and HTTPS monitors.
---@field expected_codes? string|distilled.Null The expected HTTP response code or code range of the health check. This parameter is only valid for HTTP and HTTPS monitors.
---@field follow_redirects? boolean|distilled.Null Follow redirects if returned by the origin. This parameter is only valid for HTTP and HTTPS monitors.
---@field header? cloudflare.load_balancers.MonitorsGetResponseHeaderMap|distilled.Null The HTTP request headers to send in the health check. It is recommended you set a Host header by default. The User-Agent header cannot be overridden. This parameter is only valid for HTTP and HTTPS monitors.
---@field interval? number|distilled.Null The interval between each health check. Shorter intervals may improve failover time, but will increase load on the origins as we check from multiple locations.
---@field method? string|distilled.Null The method to use for the health check. This defaults to 'GET' for HTTP/HTTPS based checks and 'connection_established' for TCP based health checks.
---@field modified_on? string|distilled.Null
---@field path? string|distilled.Null The endpoint path you want to conduct a health check against. This parameter is only valid for HTTP and HTTPS monitors.
---@field port? number|distilled.Null The port number to connect to for the health check. Required for TCP, UDP, and SMTP checks. HTTP and HTTPS checks should only define the port when using a non-standard port (HTTP: default 80, HTTPS: default 443).
---@field probe_zone? string|distilled.Null Assign this monitor to emulate the specified zone while probing. This parameter is only valid for HTTP and HTTPS monitors.
---@field retries? number|distilled.Null The number of retries to attempt in case of a timeout before marking the origin as unhealthy. Retries are attempted immediately.
---@field timeout? number|distilled.Null The timeout (in seconds) before marking the health check as failed.
---@field type? cloudflare.load_balancers.MonitorsGetResponseType|distilled.Null The protocol to use for the health check. Currently supported protocols are 'HTTP','HTTPS', 'TCP', 'ICMP-PING', 'UDP-ICMP', and 'SMTP'.

